---
/**
 * Editorial narrative drawn from the existing site's own framing:
 * Houston heat overworks cooling systems; small faults compound;
 * a dependable contractor is the fix.
 */
---

<section class="section problem" id="story" aria-labelledby="problem-title">
  <div class="container-site">
    <p class="type-label type-label--heat eyebrow" data-reveal="fade">The Houston problem</p>

    <h2 class="type-h1 problem-title" id="problem-title" data-reveal>
      Houston summers don’t <em>break</em> air conditioners.
      They <em>find</em> the weak point, then work on it all season long.
    </h2>

    <div class="problem-grid">
      <p class="type-lede" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="0.1">
        Hot weather forces a system to run longer. Filters clog faster, debris builds at the
        outdoor fan, and the whole system overworks just to hold temperature. It shows up first
        on your utility bill, then in lost cooling power.
      </p>
      <p class="type-lede" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="0.18">
        Slight malfunctions worsen when ignored, and the damage spreads to other components.
        The earlier a trained eye sees it, the smaller the repair. That’s the whole case for
        having one dependable crew who knows your system.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="problem-temps" data-reveal-group aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="temp-scale">
        <div class="temp-bar" data-reveal-child>
          <span class="temp-fill temp-fill--outside"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="temp-labels">
          <span class="type-label">Outside · Houston August</span>
          <span class="temp-num temp-num--heat"><span data-count="98" data-count-suffix="°">0°</span></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="temp-arrow" data-reveal-child>
        <span class="type-label">One working system</span>
        <svg width="52" height="20" viewBox="0 0 52 20" fill="none"><path d="M2 10h44m0 0-7-7m7 7-7 7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      </div>
      <div class="temp-scale">
        <div class="temp-bar" data-reveal-child>
          <span class="temp-fill temp-fill--inside"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="temp-labels">
          <span class="type-label">Inside · your living room</span>
          <span class="temp-num temp-num--cool"><span data-count="72" data-count-suffix="°">0°</span></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .problem-title {
    max-width: 24ch;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .problem-title em {
    font-style: normal;
    color: var(--color-heat);
  }
  .problem-grid {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.75rem;
    max-width: 70rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .problem-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 3rem;
    }
  }

  .problem-temps {
    margin-top: 4.5rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: end;
  }
  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .problem-temps {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr;
      gap: 3rem;
    }
  }
  .temp-bar {
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    background: var(--color-line-soft);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .temp-fill {
    display: block;
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
  .temp-fill--outside {
    width: 96%;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--color-warn), var(--color-heat));
  }
  .temp-fill--inside {
    width: 44%;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--color-cool-bright), var(--color-cool));
  }
  .temp-labels {
    margin-top: 0.9rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .temp-num {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4vw, 3.4rem);
    font-weight: 640;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .temp-num--heat {
    color: var(--color-heat);
  }
  .temp-num--cool {
    color: var(--color-cool);
  }
  .temp-arrow {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-faint);
    padding-bottom: 1rem;
  }
</style>
